  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "All four completed experiments use singleprofile; the multiprofile dimension (and its associated aggregation choice) is entirely unexplored, representing the largest source of uncertainty. The best-performing config so far is config_024 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted; acc 0.5375). config_017 is the most direct extension of that configuration: it changes only the profile setting to multiprofile and adds avgpool aggregation, while keeping the same RNA encoder, image encoder, and weighted fusion. This isolates the effect of multiprofile + simple aggregation. If it improves over 0.5375, multiprofile is a promising direction to further explore (e.g., transformer aggregation); if it degrades, we learn that the single-profile scvi representation is already sufficient and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or image encoder variants. Under a limited budget, testing the simplest multiprofile variant first is more informative than jumping to a complex transformer aggregation, because it establishes a clean baseline for the aggregation axis."
}

